{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice","id":1388268,"title":"Coterie Embraced a Kinfolk: Advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-14T01:37:42-07:00","id":1388268,"title":"Coterie Embraced a Kinfolk: Advice","content":"In the game I run my players threw a curve at me. A friend of the teen that they're Guardian/Adopted parent of was suffering nightmares, bouts of temper, feeling like they were being watched. The kid was a kinfolk on the verge of turning into a garou and their first change and was being observed by a pack of bone gnawers.<br /> <br /> The idea was they would take the kid in for a few days, keep an eye on him, get attacked, and either fend off the lupines or, more likely, take the kid and run from these mysterious pursuers. They would harry and herd them and then when they were pinned he would undergo his first change and they would subdue him and then the older lupines would take him away.<br /> <br /> Instead, thinking the kid was marked and now both the kid and their teen were in the know about things supernatural and what little they did know about lupines being that they can be relentless, decided to embrace them to give them an edge in survival. I figured it would be a slim chance that the embrace would stick, kinfolk being resilient/blessed against such things. I rolled and the kid survived the embrace.<br /> <br /> Thoughts and opinions would be welcome. What would the lupine's response be? Retaliation and rage seems appropriate, but what scale? Full on war? Does this include just that one pack or does it include all of the bone gnawers in the Culver City/Greater Los Angeles area? Also, what about the other vampires in the area? Will it drag others into the mess?<br /> <br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T03:31:05-07:00","id":1388285,"title":"","content":"you should probably ask in the WtA forum as well,<br /> you'll get better answers there<br /> <br /> from what little I know, embracing a kinfolk will get you hunted by the werewolf responsible for said kinfolk, not the entire tribe (of course, if there are other garou hunting vampires, they might join the party)<br /> <br /> the werewolf will focus on the sire (assuming that they know which one it is), but won't hesitate to tear down any other vampire on the way,<br /> there are no repercussions for killing vampires, other garou won't really care","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T03:32:15-07:00","id":1388286,"title":"","content":"My advice is to note that while the Garou family of said Kinfolk will want to kill the vampires who turned them, they'd be more interested in killing the Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Because Garou suck that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T05:53:11-07:00","id":1388306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1388286#post1388286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Garou suck that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, at that point it's a security issue, who knows what secrets the kin folk knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T06:33:01-07:00","id":1388319,"title":"","content":"I... I don't think he can go through with his first change now. He's just a regular vampire, maybe with some supernatural flaws. At this point, the Garou would want to kill the players and the kin for the purpose of honour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T07:26:30-07:00","id":1388328,"title":"","content":"So my best guess is, the pack of bone gnawers, led by the werewolf directly responsible for the kinfolk will do anything they can to kill the kinfolk and either the vampire responsible or at least enough vampires to make them think they must've gotten the one responsible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T07:53:23-07:00","id":1388333,"title":"","content":"Just get them to make new characters, it will be quicker. In the garous eyes they not only murdered a cub but brought it back as a twisted parody of itself instead of letting it's spirit return to the Mother. They be dead....that said. Murdering the kid in order to embrace should have brought on First Change out of survival reflex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T09:45:44-07:00","id":1388347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1388306#post1388306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, at that point it's a security issue, who knows what secrets the kin folk knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought this was implied, but just for context, the kid didn't know he was kinfolk.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T10:18:47-07:00","id":1388350,"title":"","content":"As said, the Garou's priorities would likely be:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The kinfolk</li> <li>The Sire</li> <li>The Sire's coeterie</li> <li>Any kindred within clawing distance</li> <li>The friend who led Wyrm-tainted beings to one of their kinfolk</li> <li>Whatever they're supposed to be hunting</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> Unless the PC's are incredibly good at killing things or going into hiding they're probably dead. Best thing for them to do would be to skip town before the Bone Gnawers pick up their scent, maybe settle somewhere in Poland for the next couple of decades, so they're probably dead already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T10:35:27-07:00","id":1388356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1388347#post1388347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought this was implied, but just for context, the kid didn't know he was kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the wolves know he's kin? If they don't then the matter is kinda moot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T11:02:08-07:00","id":1388364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1388356#post1388356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do the wolves know he's kin? If they don't then the matter is kinda moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>They knew and they knew that he didn't know. They were waiting for him to change (and from their POV if he didn't they would have guided him into the community later).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T11:39:40-07:00","id":1388373,"title":"","content":"The werewolves will try to kill the players for corrupting their kinfolk and try to kill their kinfolk out of mercy. They may or may go get other packs to help out, or they might try to do it themselves because of honor and all that, just depends on what kind of a story you want to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T12:07:34-07:00","id":1388383,"title":"","content":"I don't want them to die, but I want to them to feel the weight of their actions.<br /> <br /> At the moment I am thinking that it will be just the pack that was watching the kid who will seek retribution. The others of the tribe viewing it as their duty to do the killing. The rest of the tribe having other concerns. As I understand it vampires a concern of the lupines, but not high on priority list.<br /> <br /> Also, something I should have remembered sooner, there is a 4th gen meth lurking in the shadows with an interest in the coterie's unlives. She might have to flex her influence a bit more directly sooner than anticipated.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T12:35:38-07:00","id":1388392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1388383#post1388383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want them to die, but I want to them to feel the weight of their actions.<br /> <br /> At the moment I am thinking that it will be just the pack that was watching the kid who will seek retribution. The others of the tribe viewing it as their duty to do the killing. The rest of the tribe having other concerns. As I understand it vampires a concern of the lupines, but not high on priority list.<br /> <br /> Also, something I should have remembered sooner, there is a 4th gen meth lurking in the shadows with an interest in the coterie's unlives. She might have to flex her influence a bit more directly sooner than anticipated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of ways you could do it. If you don't want the players to deal with a full pack of werewolves, Maybe have one of the werewolves, to whom the kid was a relative, tell the other pack members, &quot;I'll handle this.&quot; Cue mini-arc of players trying to get away from a very angry werewolf. Maybe the players have to go find some renowned werewolf hunting vampire and trade in a boon to get his help. Maybe it turns out the werewolves were also being tracked and the players get contacted by someone (or someones) who are interested in killing the werewolves (Pentex? Black Spirals? Skindancers? Sabbat? Some equally stomach-churning group) and are willing to temporarily ally with the players to take care of the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T12:41:48-07:00","id":1388394,"title":"","content":"Obviously the specifics depend on edition, but generally involving Lupines in a way that leads to combat is a nuclear option for most vampire games. Using a pack of Lupines who are at home in the city, which is supposed to be a vampires home court advantage.... that goes from nuclear option to planet cracking/exterminatus grade weaponry. Unless the players are very tactically minded IRL or have some of the most combat OP builds, there is no way to have this fight and not have a lot of final deaths.<br /> <br /> The automatic kill everything response most lupines have for vampires is just not a good thing to mess with in most stories. Often the other changing breeds tend to be a better fit for interacting with vampires, the were-spiders for instance tend to be more accepting.<br /> <br /> So let's look at the situation.<br /> 1. Every vampire in the city is marked for death by virtue of being a vampire.<br /> 2. Every coterie member is marked for death for being in part responsible for the corruption of the kinfolk.<br /> 3. If something as wyrm tainted as a 4th generation is in the area multiple high rank packs are going to be hunting the area.<br /> 4. The Bone Gnawers might be a degenerate group of lupines but even they wouldn't willingly leave a kinfolk with vampires, regardless of their chance at changing.<br /> 5. Since the Bone Gnawers pack messed up by letting the kinfolk get embraced, they might be facing repercussions from the packs hunting the 4th generation.<br /> 6. 4th generation Methuselahs are like black holes, they have a gravity well that pulls in other high level characters that utterly out class normal characters and thus dominate the story.<br /> <br /> In short everyone is going to die. It might have been safer to plan a story where everyones survival was based off of a nitroglycerin juggling contest in the middle of gasoline and fireworks storage warehouse during an earthquake.<br /> <br /> Yes it sounds like most people are over stating the dire end results, but each aspect of the story seems to be too big for what you were wanting to do with it. If you want a lupine to be a threat but not an almost automatic TPK, then you use a single one, not a pack. If you want the vampires to be able to retreat then you use a lupine tribe that is hampered by the city rather than being at home in it (use a red talon rather than bone gnawer), if you want an elder who could be a safety net you use a 6th or 7th generation with a lot of XP rather than a meth one step below antediluvian.<br /> <br /> If you want to maintain any hint of &quot;realism&quot; with the game either make this a one shot where everyone dies and the story is about how you choose your end, or you come up with an even bigger conflict that makes all those involved change priorities, but you are already messing with 4th generations so bigger would be what, the actual Apocalypse/Gehenna hitting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T13:26:59-07:00","id":1388411,"title":"","content":"If this is a crossover and you have mages in the game, a mage could be very useful in allowing the vampires to escape. A Technocracy mage might have an understanding with a powerful vampire such as the Methuselah, or even be their ghoul (because Methuselahs break the game). A Nephandi would certainly love to see werewolves fail in stopping their plan for mass carnage--but that would be a devil's bargain for the PCs if they get their help.<br /> <br /> I think the real question is, how hard do you want to come down on the players?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T14:00:13-07:00","id":1388422,"title":"","content":"The encounter with the kid and lupines was supposed to be one off scenario that might lead to something in the future.<br /> <br /> The players and the characters are largely ignorant of lupines. Just rumors and so forth.<br /> The 4th gen is a BBEG for late game.<br /> <br /> They are on good terms with Nines Rodriguez and an angry pack of werewolves is a danger to everyone. Hmm...<br /> <br /> How about this: Word gets to the ears of the Barons, possible from a minion of the 4th Gen. They start arguing about what to do. The PCs try to convince them to help or give them some kind of resources. During this time the sire of one of the PCs (Who is a mole for the Cam) offers to get some outside help for them in exchange for some favors. They get help from one side or the other with favors to be owed later and let the PCs come up with some kind of plan then pit their plan against the lupine tactics and see what shakes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T14:08:30-07:00","id":1388428,"title":"","content":"To the OP: most Garou would would consider the kinfolk dead, mourn him/her loss, then hunt him/she down, before doing the same with a vengeance for the leeches responsible for tainting one of their own...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T17:49:42-07:00","id":1388506,"title":"","content":"Your coterie needs to properly understand what they did: they murdered a kid because it was the easy option. Not only did they murdered them but they also cut them off from a greater world forever and irrevocably. And then they damned this shell of a spirit crippled child to a hellish parasitic parody of life. Then worry about the kids relatives who are rightfully upset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T18:17:26-07:00","id":1388512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1388506#post1388506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your coterie needs to properly understand what they did: they murdered a kid because it was the easy option. Not only did they murdered them but they also cut them off from a greater world forever and irrevocably. And then they damned this shell of a spirit crippled child to a hellish parasitic parody of life. Then worry about the kids relatives who are rightfully upset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nicely put.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T20:07:46-07:00","id":1388545,"title":"","content":"Let the players think they got away with it until the last game session of your story. Then WHAM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T20:55:48-07:00","id":1388548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1388545#post1388545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let the players think they got away with it until the last game session of your story. Then WHAM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh heh. Nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T00:44:30-07:00","id":1388593,"title":"","content":"Technically you are Garou from birth, and not Kinfolk if you are able to have a first change. In revised one of the questions answered by the Authors/Developer was that yes Scent of the True form works on detecting if a baby was Kinfolk or Garou. A lot of the W20 were kind of new at that stage of development and they didn't realize this when they talked about Kin Fetches. Kin Fetches weren't designed as a detection system for Garou, they were designed so that Garou could have normal Lives away from danger and when they had their first change their Kin Fetches would make sure they get found and trained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T01:53:31-07:00","id":1388605,"title":"","content":"If werewolves weren't intended to be a major part of your campaign and the players aren't intimately aware of the setting then you can always make the pack exactly as scary as you want it to be and not worry too much about getting everything perfect.<br /> That said there's loads of good advice above and ways to make game out of it.<br /> Do the pack know where the new vampire is and which Vampire embraced them?<br /> Are they going to start grilling the new vampires friends to try and find them?<br /> Are they going to start randomly killing any vampire they can find on the street in the hopes of getting to the right one?<br /> How are the other kindred in the city going to react now that the local Werewolves have gone on a killing spree? Can they negotiate a truce and what will they have to sacrifice (probably literally)?<br /> <br /> If you want to keep it away from muder then you could end up in a situation where the players are managing negotiations with the pack, offering up some random Caitiff as the guilty party and owing the barons a whole pile of boons. In this case negotiations may well just be the coterie giving the location of the &quot;Guilty&quot; coterie's haven to the pack. The players aren't dead, but they are seriously in debt to their elders, other kindred are asking awkward questions about where they were when the new kindred was embraced and they've chosen which of the baron's enemies got thrown under the bus. Oh and the new kindred vampire has to die, preferably at the claws of it's mother/father/uncle who's screaming in rage/sorrow at what's been done to their baby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:33:02-07:00","id":1388614,"title":"","content":"Uriah Travers is a canon character from Nueva Orleans by Night who is kinfolk and was embraced by a Malkavian. Uriah is a Vampire, because he did not change before the embrace, but he believes being a werewolf because he knows protean and he is influenced by the moon blood. Other kinfolk vampire are the Dunsirn from the Giovanni/Hecata and the revenant family of Danislavs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T04:21:42-07:00","id":1388640,"title":"","content":"In &quot;Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes&quot; was a story idea about Embraced Kinfolk, where other Kinfolks were ordered to kill this unfortunate and the one who was responsible for that. But in many cities there's a non aggression pact between Garou and Cainites (p. ex. Chicago). So it's really up to you.<br /> <br /> Eldagusto, I don't think that Scent the True Form can detect Kinfolk of Garou before First Change (even it the authors said so). If they are right then how they explain so much Lost Cubs?<br /> <br /> And I don't think that hiding in Poland is a good option. We have Garou septs here too \ud83d\ude1c. And they are more traditionalist than the North America's ones so basically ANY Cainite unfortunately enough to meet local Garou will meet his Final Death too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 05-15-2020, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T04:29:02-07:00","id":1388641,"title":"","content":"I think its important not to overstate things as well.<br /> <br /> There's a sickly awesome scene in UNDER A BLOOD RED MOON where the Garou come back home from a successful day of vampire hunting and proceed to find the family they've been staying with has been Embraced. Well, most of the family was Embraced. The mommy, daddy, and the baby with the intermediate children having been left as meals for them while they're Dominated into ignoring it. It's a horrifying psychological attack by the Sabbat against them.<br /> <br /> And you know what? THE SABBAT GET AWAY WITH IT.<br /> <br /> The Garou never will find out Wendy Wade and Phillip Riguard as well as their goons because the war goes on. It's just a reminder that the war has casualties and worse, the losses there are going to just be another add on to the pile they have in their eternal war against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I always found that a very interesting thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T06:35:48-07:00","id":1388664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1388641#post1388641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think its important not to overstate things as well.<br /> <br /> There's a sickly awesome scene in UNDER A BLOOD RED MOON where the Garou come back home from a successful day of vampire hunting and proceed to find the family they've been staying with has been Embraced. Well, most of the family was Embraced. The mommy, daddy, and the baby with the intermediate children having been left as meals for them while they're Dominated into ignoring it. It's a horrifying psychological attack by the Sabbat against them.<br /> <br /> And you know what? THE SABBAT GET AWAY WITH IT.<br /> <br /> The Garou never will find out Wendy Wade and Phillip Riguard as well as their goons because the war goes on. It's just a reminder that the war has casualties and worse, the losses there are going to just be another add on to the pile they have in their eternal war against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I always found that a very interesting thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but that was during the war and I think it's another story. I think the idea was that this unfortunate Kinfolk/Garou was Embraced during the time of relative peace, when Garou occasionally kill or at least mostly ignore Cainites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T06:39:11-07:00","id":1388665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1388664#post1388664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, but that was during the war and I think it's another story. I think the idea was that this unfortunate Kinfolk/Garou was Embraced during the time of relative peace, when Garou occasionally kill or at least mostly ignore Cainites.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but even then, Kinfolk die a lot and there's always a war going on for the Garou. So, unlike Kindred, they can't devote extensive resources to a vengeance quest.<br /> <br /> It's on the list but it's a very long list:<br /> <br /> * Save the World []<br /> * Destroy Pentex []<br /> * Destroy Black Spiral Dancers []<br /> * Destroy Seventh Generation [Check]<br /> * Continue War of Rage in the Amazon [Check]<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> So the PCs will be marked for death if identified but the Garou can't go for revenge for long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T07:27:34-07:00","id":1388674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1388665#post1388665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True but even then, Kinfolk die a lot and there's always a war going on for the Garou. So, unlike Kindred, they can't devote extensive resources to a vengeance quest.<br /> <br /> It's on the list but it's a very long list:<br /> <br /> * Save the World []<br /> * Destroy Pentex []<br /> * Destroy Black Spiral Dancers []<br /> * Destroy Seventh Generation [Check]<br /> * Continue War of Rage in the Amazon [Check]<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> So the PCs will be marked for death if identified but the Garou can't go for revenge for long.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But that's why Kinfolks are for \ud83d\ude09. They could also hunt Embraced Kinfolk and its Sire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T09:17:19-07:00","id":1388963,"title":"","content":"<u><b>&quot;This is ridiculous! What am I doing here? I'm in the wrong story!&quot; -the Baker's Wife, Into the Woods, Stephen Sondheim</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> First, a couple of points. Don't think of them as criticism, but just some friendly comments from a critic. So, umm, yeah. Definitionally, they're criticisms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice#post1388268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the game I run my players threw a curve at me. A friend of the teen that they're Guardian/Adopted parent of was suffering nightmares, bouts of temper, feeling like they were being watched. The kid was a kinfolk on the verge of turning into a garou and their first change and was being observed by a pack of bone gnawers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you familiar with Chekhov's Gun? If not, look <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chekhov%27s_gun\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. It has been preached again and again on gaming forums for years... decades. Economy of detail. If there is a story element introduced, be prepared for it to matter because you're the one who put it there. Most of what players do in a game is sit there trying to figure out which parts matter and which don't. You gave them this kid, which implied he mattered. From the players' perspective, they were doing what you wanted.<br /> <br /> Once Garou were introduced to the story, Garou existed. It's a little like the genie and the lamp; you wished them into existence, now deal with it.<br /> <br /> It's also why cross-overs are a bad idea, but going on a tangent in which my player's pcs were turned into garden gnome statues would violate... wait for it... economy of detail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice#post1388268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea was they would take the kid in for a few days, keep an eye on him, get attacked, and either fend off the lupines or, more likely, take the kid and run from these mysterious pursuers. They would harry and herd them and then when they were pinned he would undergo his first change and they would subdue him and then the older lupines would take him away.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, this is why railroading your players is a bad idea. Not just because it makes for a boring game where the players feel like their choices don't matter, but because said railroad never, ever runs on time. You run the game world, but players run the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice#post1388268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, thinking the kid was marked and now both the kid and their teen were in the know about things supernatural and what little they did know about lupines being that they can be relentless, decided to embrace them to give them an edge in survival. I figured it would be a slim chance that the embrace would stick, kinfolk being resilient/blessed against such things. I rolled and the kid survived the embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, over the loudspeakers the station manager just announced, &quot;The 4:10 to Yuma will be leaving track 7 at midnight, an express bound for Tokyo. All aboard!&quot;<br /> <br /> Your next mistake was rolling for it. Do you roll to see if gravity still works? Do you roll to see if the Atlantic Ocean is still wet? You did not want the embrace to stick, it shouldn't have stuck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice#post1388268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts and opinions would be welcome. What would the lupine's response be? Retaliation and rage seems appropriate, but what scale? Full on war? Does this include just that one pack or does it include all of the bone gnawers in the Culver City/Greater Los Angeles area? Also, what about the other vampires in the area? Will it drag others into the mess?<br /> <br /> Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Deep breath. We're all friends here. Come in off that ledge. Here. Have a warm beverage. Should I turn on some <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LTrk4X9ACtw\" target=\"_blank\">calming music</a>?<br /> <br /> Your chronicle is not ruined. You don't need to kill the whole party. This can be salvaged.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ideas:</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Dirty Cops </b>Not every Garou is a paragon of honor. The Bone Gnawers were a pack that was on thin-ice to begin with. In losing track of this kid --their one and only duty for the sept-- they fucked up big time. They will kill the kid. They will tell themselves it is to put him out of his misery, not to cover up their failure. Killing witnesses and destroying all physical evidence is just... umm, protecting the veil or something. It's totally not that they panicked. Where will they claim the kid went? Who knows, it's no longer the players' problem. (cf &quot;economy of detail&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Clap if you believe in Lupines</b>! This is VtM, where &quot;Garou&quot; do not exist, but &quot;Lupines&quot; do exist. Very different creatures. The players may have read every WtA book ever written. One player might even have a tribe glyph tattooed on their leg. Doesn't matter. The pcs know nothing about Lupines. Are Lupines organized, or psychotic marauders? Are they inflexible, or willing to deal? Who knows? Only you! I suggest that in your world Lupines believe Gaia preserves those who deserve the first change. The unworthy die before then. This is not unreasonable given the appalling rate of infant mortality prior to 1900, and Lupines seeming disregard for pointless comabt. Your Lupines shrug and figure the kid was weak and deserved to die. Cold, man, cold, but remember the weak make lousy warriors.<br /> <br /> <b>Crossing the Glienicke Bridge </b>The Lupines and the Kindred of LA had a treaty, which forbids killing full members of the other species in enemy territory. Both sides would like to continue to have a treaty. Some Shadow Lords kill the Bone Gnawers for failing to hide the kid, who was not technically covered under the treaty since he was in vampire-land. They also demand the lives of the coterie, so they can claim some sort of victory. (Consequences, dammit!) This now becomes a more manageable story of vampire v. vampire as the coterie has to convince other vampires not to hand them over. In the end, the Shadow Lords will accept any vampires the coterie can round up... or embrace; they just need the body count, not justice. Use this to thin out your cast list. (nb economy of detail)<br /> <br /> <b>What Rough Beast...? </b>The kid looks dead at first, but Abominations are weird like that. The kid arises, in Crinos form with vampiric disciplines, but Humanity zero and in permanent frenzy. &quot;This is bad, this is bad, this is very, very bad!&quot;, says everybody on both sides. Actually, &quot;shouts everyone&quot;, as they run away. The Bone Gnawers and the coterie realize they have created a monster, that must be destroyed. The next session is a bug-hunt which looks a lot like the movie Alien. Everyone works together to end this... Abomination. One session, then it's over. Make sure the Bone Gnawers all die, so no other Lupines hear what happened.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T10:18:44-07:00","id":1388981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1388963#post1388963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[U][B]<br /> <br /> Your chronicle is not ruined. You don't need to kill the whole party. This can be salvaged.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ideas:</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Dirty Cops </b>Not every Garou is a paragon of honor. The Bone Gnawers were a pack that was on thin-ice to begin with. In losing track of this kid --their one and only duty for the sept-- they fucked up big time. They will kill the kid. They will tell themselves it is to put him out of his misery, not to cover up their failure. Killing witnesses and destroying all physical evidence is just... umm, protecting the veil or something. It's totally not that they panicked. Where will they claim the kid went? Who knows, it's no longer the players' problem. (cf &quot;economy of detail&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Clap if you believe in Lupines</b>! This is VtM, where &quot;Garou&quot; do not exist, but &quot;Lupines&quot; do exist. Very different creatures. The players may have read every WtA book ever written. One player might even have a tribe glyph tattooed on their leg. Doesn't matter. The pcs know nothing about Lupines. Are Lupines organized, or psychotic marauders? Are they inflexible, or willing to deal? Who knows? Only you! I suggest that in your world Lupines believe Gaia preserves those who deserve the first change. The unworthy die before then. This is not unreasonable given the appalling rate of infant mortality prior to 1900, and Lupines seeming disregard for pointless comabt. Your Lupines shrug and figure the kid was weak and deserved to die. Cold, man, cold, but remember the weak make lousy warriors.<br /> <br /> <b>Crossing the Glienicke Bridge </b>The Lupines and the Kindred of LA had a treaty, which forbids killing full members of the other species in enemy territory. Both sides would like to continue to have a treaty. Some Shadow Lords kill the Bone Gnawers for failing to hide the kid, who was not technically covered under the treaty since he was in vampire-land. They also demand the lives of the coterie, so they can claim some sort of victory. (Consequences, dammit!) This now becomes a more manageable story of vampire v. vampire as the coterie has to convince other vampires not to hand them over. In the end, the Shadow Lords will accept any vampires the coterie can round up... or embrace; they just need the body count, not justice. Use this to thin out your cast list. (nb economy of detail)<br /> <br /> <b>What Rough Beast...? </b>The kid looks dead at first, but Abominations are weird like that. The kid arises, in Crinos form with vampiric disciplines, but Humanity zero and in permanent frenzy. &quot;This is bad, this is bad, this is very, very bad!&quot;, says everybody on both sides. Actually, &quot;shouts everyone&quot;, as they run away. The Bone Gnawers and the coterie realize they have created a monster, that must be destroyed. The next session is a bug-hunt which looks a lot like the movie Alien. Everyone works together to end this... Abomination. One session, then it's over. Make sure the Bone Gnawers all die, so no other Lupines hear what happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>All good points. What is this treaty? Another poster had mentioned a non-aggression pact.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T11:54:37-07:00","id":1389022,"title":"","content":"There is no canon treaty in Los Angeles. New Orleans by Night had a Lupine-Leech treaty, though, so there is precedent.<br /> <br /> If it were my chronicle, I'd say the vampires and lupines drew up a treaty years ago. They divvied up Los Angeles. Each are allowed to pass through the others' territory. No permanent homes or vamp/wolf violence allowed if you're on foreign territory, though terra nullis is fair play. The rules only apply to the splats themselves, not kinfolk or ghouls. Vamps can feed anywhere, if they're discreet. Lupines can blow up all the oil refineries they want.<br /> <br /> Where are the lines? It doesn't matter. They are wherever you need them to be to prevent the pcs from ever, ever needing to go there again. This effectively writes Lupines out of your chronicle. At a guess, I'd say Simi Valley, Thousand Oaks, and, obviously, everything east of the 15 belong to the Lupines. Angeles National Forest is almost too obvious to mention.<br /> <br /> One successful Politics roll will allow a member of the coterie to &quot;remember&quot; this treaty. Except, never mind. Never, never hinge your plot on a single roll unless you are willing to follow through. (Learning is fun!)<br /> <br /> This keeps the Lupines existing in the world, but out of the story.<br /> <br /> You tell me the details. It's your chronicle. OTOH, maybe don't have details, so you can make it up as you go along. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T12:05:02-07:00","id":1389024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1389022#post1389022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no canon treaty in Los Angeles. New Orleans by Night had a Lupine-Leech treaty, though, so there is precedent.<br /> <br /> If it were my chronicle, I'd say the vampires and lupines drew up a treaty years ago. They divvied up Los Angeles. Each are allowed to pass through the others' territory. No permanent homes or vamp/wolf violence allowed if you're on foreign territory, though terra nullis is fair play. The rules only apply to the splats themselves, not kinfolk or ghouls. Vamps can feed anywhere, if they're discreet. Lupines can blow up all the oil refineries they want.<br /> <br /> Where are the lines? It doesn't matter. They are wherever you need them to be to prevent the pcs from ever, ever needing to go there again. This effectively writes Lupines out of your chronicle. At a guess, I'd say Simi Valley, Thousand Oaks, and, obviously, everything east of the 15 belong to the Lupines. Angeles National Forest is almost too obvious to mention.<br /> <br /> One successful Politics roll will allow a member of the coterie to &quot;remember&quot; this treaty. Except, never mind. Never, never hinge your plot on a single roll unless you are willing to follow through. (Learning is fun!)<br /> <br /> This keeps the Lupines existing in the world, but out of the story.<br /> <br /> You tell me the details. It's your chronicle. OTOH, maybe don't have details, so you can make it up as you go along. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Since they went there I wanted there to be a chance of it happening. Player agency and all that, especially since the sire lost humanity over it and it does lead to story opportunities. They are now being thrust into larger kindred politics and this will bring one of the character's sire's back into their unlife.<br /> <br /> In my defense I would say it was less of a railroad and more of a failure on my part to anticipate player possibilities.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:44:19-07:00","id":1389117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388268-coterie-embraced-a-kinfolk-advice?p=1389024#post1389024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my defense I would say it was less of a railroad and more of a failure on my part to anticipate player possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that has happened to every ST, GM, and DM in the hobby.<br /> <br /> It happens.<br /> <br /> Did I mention my coterie of statues? I decided to cross-over a Euthanatos mage who revered Greek myths. All rotes emulated a mythical figure's powers... Hercules, Sirens, Delphic Oracle, etc. I only thought of medusa when the pcs started buying mirrors. (My out, btw, was that they reverted at the next sunset, per usual. They took out the mage with a sniper rifle.)<br /> <br /> As far as player agency goes, yes, players should control their characters. You, however, control the rest of the world. As long as you don't directly contradict any previously established facts of the world, it is fair play. In the normal course of play the ST is constantly expanding the universe. That bar they went to for the first time? It didn't exist last week. That cabbie they fed on, but rolled a botch? He wasn't a gangster's brother until they rolled. The chandelier filled with burning candles in the Prince's haven hanging from a weak chain? The chain was fine until a pc rolled a critical success on an attack roll.<br /> <br /> All fair play.<br /> <br /> Bottom lining on this, what brought your original post to the forum was how to handle things now that a story element got out of control and threatened to derail the story altogether. My advice? As much as possible <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PutOnABus\" target=\"_blank\">write the Lupines out of the story due to previously unknown outside curcumstances</a> or <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OnceMoreWithClarity\" target=\"_blank\">explain them as being something manageable</a>, while not making it <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CliffhangerCopout\" target=\"_blank\">too, too obvious</a><br /> <br /> Or, have the pcs massacred in a tpk. I'm guessing the <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PlotArmor\" target=\"_blank\">players would rather lose their agency than their characters</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}